{"symbol":"CYCS","resolved":{"input":"CYCS","symbol":"CYCS","ncbi_gene_id":"54205","name":"cytochrome c, somatic","location":"7p15.3","aliases":["CYC","HCS","THC4"],"uniprot":"P99999","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"CYCS function (UniProt P99999, UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot reviewed annotation without a specific evidence code): Electron carrier protein. The oxidized form of the cytochrome c heme group can accept an electron from the heme group of the cytochrome c1 subunit of cytochrome reductase. Cytochrome c then transfers this electron to the cytochrome oxidase complex, the final protein carrier in the mitochondrial electron-transport chain","evidence":"curated database evidence","code":"CUR","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P99999","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P99999/entry","title":"CYCS: Cytochrome c"}]},{"text":"CYCS function (UniProt P99999, UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot reviewed annotation without a specific evidence code): Plays a role in apoptosis. Suppression of the anti-apoptotic members or activation of the pro-apoptotic members of the Bcl-2 family leads to altered mitochondrial membrane permeability resulting in release of cytochrome c into the cytosol. Binding of cytochrome c to Apaf-1 triggers the activation of caspase-9, which then accelerates apoptosis by activating other caspases","evidence":"curated database evidence","code":"CUR","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P99999","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P99999/entry","title":"CYCS: Cytochrome c"}]}],"go":[{"text":"CYCS GO biological process annotations: cellular respiration, execution phase of apoptosis, intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway","evidence":"curated database evidence","code":"CUR","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P99999","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P99999/entry","title":"CYCS: Cytochrome c"}]},{"text":"CYCS GO biological process annotations: apoptotic signaling pathway, mitochondrial electron transport, cytochrome c to oxygen, mitochond